# ADR-deviation marker — feat/194-pre-tag-version-sync-guardrails
- date: 2026-09-21
- branch: feat/194-pre-tag-version-sync-guardrails
- adr_governing: ADR-004 (publish pipeline safety contract)
- outcome: ADR-honored

The change extends ADR-004's pre-publish check surface earlier in the
pipeline. The `release: published` trigger + two-job checks/publish shape
+ trusted-publisher OIDC path + `--ignore-scripts` discipline all remain
intact. The new PR-CI workflow runs a NARROWER check (version-sync only)
at PR time. The existing release-time checks still fire.

Every invariant ADR-004 names holds:
- Tag ancestry check at publish time — unchanged
- dist/lite/ presence assertion at publish time — unchanged
- Andon scan + tier filter at publish time — unchanged
- Trusted publisher + provenance — unchanged
- Environment gate on npm-publish — unchanged

No new ADR filed. This is an additive earlier layer, not a decision change.
